  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all thermal incidents must be reported within 24 hours and affected customers notified within 72 hours. S2 sets a 55°C test with a permanent 7% failure limit, per-model results to customers and regulators but no public per-model publication, and no automatic sales stop. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit deadline where feasible with owner notice; S4 requires built-in suppression within 36 months. S5 triggers corrective action and independent review above 8/100k, with mandatory recall only if the regulator confirms ongoing serious risk or failed corrective action, and notices are prompt."
